OL,3,GNEWSAHidden manuscripts reveal medieval
OL,4,Areading habits
OL,5,
OL,6,FSeventeen fragments of medieval
OL,7,Fmanuscripts that had been "hidden in
OL,8,Fplain sight" for centuries have been
OL,9,Funcovered in Guernsey.
OL,11,FOffering insight into the island's
OL,12,Fearly literary culture, the fragments
OL,13,Fsuggest late medieval Guernsey was home
OL,14,Fto keen readers, and reading in French
OL,15,Frather than English was preferred.
OL,17,FAlso regarded as "striking early
OL,18,Fexamples of recycling", historians
OL,19,Ffound the fragments were repurposed as
OL,20,Fcovers for notebooks and bindings for
OL,21,Fadministrative records, meaning they
OL,22,Fwere unknowingly preserved.
OL,23,APub: 25-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Ch Is NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
FL,443,440,260,160,0,100
